This error suggests that there is an issue with the `apoc.util.validate` procedure in your Neo4j database. Here are some possible solutions:

1. Check if the procedure is properly installed:
   - Make sure you have the APOC Procedures library installed in your Neo4j database. You can download it from the official website (https://github.com/neo4j-contrib/neo4j-apoc-procedures) and follow the installation instructions.
   - If the library is already installed, run the following query to verify if the `apoc.util.validate` procedure is available:
     ```graphql
     {
       apocProcedureExists(name: "apoc.util.validate") {
         exists
       }
     }
     ```

2. Check if the procedure is properly registered:
   - Run the following query to see all the procedures registered in your database:
     ```graphql
     {
       db {
         procedures {
           nodes {
             name
           }
         }
       }
     }
     ```
   - Check if `apoc.util.validate` is listed among the registered procedures.
   - If it's not listed, run the following command to register it manually:
     ```cypher
     CALL gds.register('apoc', '3.5.0') YIELD success;
     ```
   - This will register the `apoc` library and make all its procedures available.

3. Check if the procedure has been called correctly:
   - Review the GraphQL query where the `apoc.util.validate` procedure is being invoked and check if the syntax is correct.
   - Make sure you're passing the correct arguments to the procedure. The `apoc.util.validate` procedure takes a single argument, which is the value to be validated.

If none of these solutions work, please refer to the official documentation of the APOC Procedures library or contact Neo4j support for further assistance.

