```javascript
function determineRelevantProtocol(inputData) {
  if (/^([\da-fA-F]{1,4}:){7}([\da-fA-F]{1,4})$/.test(inputData.sourceIP) && /^([\da-fA-F]{1,4}:){7}([\da-fA-F]{1,4})$/.test(inputData.destinationIP)) {
    // Both source and destination IP addresses are in IPv6 format
    return 'Option A';
  } else {
    // Neither source nor destination IP address is in IPv6 format
    return 'Option C'; // Default to UDP
  }
}

console.log(determineRelevantProtocol(inputData)); // Output: "Option A"
```

In this example, the regular expression `/^([\da-fA-F]{1,4}:){7}([\da-fA-F]{1,4})$/` is used to check if a string follows the format of an IPv6 address. If both the source and destination IP addresses match this pattern, then Option A (IPv6) is returned as the most relevant protocol. Otherwise, we default to Option C (UDP). You can modify the function logic based on your specific requirements.

